Guttenberg Airport in Sweden it was from  here in July 2018 that a Turkish  Airlines aircraft was scheduled to  depart for Istanbul on board a rejected  asylum seeker being deported to  Afghanistan and Swedish student Ellen  Arsen seeking to stop the flight she  broadcast her mission live from her  smartphone that's an ignored numerous  request to take a seat until the pilot  agreed to let the asylum seeker off the  plane the video was viewed millions of  times across the Internet  Nelson was celebrated by some as a hero  of civil disobedience but she also faced  a torrent of abuse  [Applause]  Elson was charged with violating  Sweden's aviation act for refusing to  comply with instructions  her lawyer contested the allegation  saying the instructions had come from  the crew rather than the pilot national  laws defined the crimes that can be  prosecuted it is clear that what  happened on July 23 did not violate any  specific law so there was no punishable  offence arson faced up to six months in  jail instead judges handed down a fine  totaling 370 euros
 

